ncomfortably true a subject that's a  little impolite or unwanted that  nonetheless needs to be said and I  promise you this committee does not set  out with a specific goal to end up with  10 scripts it would please Jim Harrison  but we do have guidelines that I think  tip the Nicholl fellowship toward  stories that have meaning we ask of  ourselves does the story have an  original premise does this script make  you feel that the writer is taking you  on a journey does the story connect with  you emotionally whether it's a comedy or  a drama or another genre does the writer  have a distinctive and original voice or  do you feel that you've seen this movie  before does the story have vivid  characters who each speak in their own  voice do you want to know what happens  to them does the story propel you  forward and do your main characters take  the actions that propel the story are  the themes of the story  thought-provoking across genres is the  story about something that might provoke  a discussion when you finish reading the  script even if it has flaws do you still  feel that there's something special  about it even if it has flaws is the key  phrase when our committee convenes we  aren't looking for perfect scripts  crafts yes  perfection absolutely not we're not even  really seeking scripts we're seeking  interesting writers  challenged people who may not yet have  nailed every aspect of screenwriting but  who have something that they absolutely  have to say we're looking for writers  who make us feel they can't be silenced  who have something on their minds who  won't settle in comfortably into a  commercial field of cookie cutter  entertainments but who will keep  bringing up the important subjects the  uncool emotions the stories that  encompass the full spectrum of all human  behavior  rewriting can always improve a script  that isn't yet perfect but nothing you  learn in film school supplies the  essential qualities of soul and heart  and courage and daring that made this  year's screenplays rise to the top of  the Nicholl fellowship competition so if  you're writing right now dig deep this  year our nickel committee Reds 6895  screenplays which through multiple  readings were narrowed down to 349  quarter-finalists out of rich rows 151  semi-finalists the semi-finalists  scripts were read by members of the  Academy across all branches again  multiple times when we had 10 finalists  our committee met for several hours  discussing all 10 writers and at the end  of a long impassioned meeting that  involved neither a beluga caviar nor  cocaine we settled on four winning  entries three individual writers plus  one writing team I'm going to ask  Jennifer Nelson to introduce those  writers to you Jennifer is a talented  and highly valued part of the nickel  committee she's a member of the short  film and animation branch she directed  Kung Fu Panda and Kung Fu Panda 2 for  which she was nominated for an Oscar  she's the only the second woman who's  ever been nominated for an animation  Oscar this year she directed the  live-action film the darkest mind and  she has directed tonight's live reading  of scenes from the Academy Nicholl  fellowship screenplays for 2018 please  welcome Jennifer you now
 

